// =============================================================================
// MRM Infotech — Dynamic Corporate Website  (schema v2)
// PostgreSQL · Prisma 6 · Repo: MRMinfotech-backend (multi-file schema: one model per file)
//
// CONVENTIONS
//  1. Big content entities (Page, Product, Service, Industry, Post, CaseStudy,
//     TeamMember, JobPosting) -> separate *Translation tables
//     (slug, SEO, publish-state differ per language).
//  2. Small child items (features, FAQs, nav labels, tags …) -> `i18n Json`
//     { "en": {...}, "bn": {...} }, validated with Zod in the API.
//  3. Languages are DATA. Every `locale` column is a real FK to Language.code,
//     so a typo can never create a ghost language, and a 3rd language needs no migration.
//  4. TRUST RULE: Client / Testimonial / CaseStudy / TrustBadge are public ONLY when
//     isVerified = true AND evidenceNote is filled. Enforced in the API AND by
//     DB CHECK constraints (see constraints.sql).
//  5. No EduManage / MediSheba operational data lives here — ever.
//  6. Everything the owner may want to change without a developer is DATA:
//     brand (Theme), logo, fonts, navigation, pages/blocks, products, services,
//     pricing, offices, announcements, email templates, forms, SEO, redirects.
//  7. Media references written as `// -> MediaAsset.id` are plain UUIDs checked by
//     the API (media-in-use guard). Theme + gallery links are real FKs.
// =============================================================================

generator client {
  provider      = "prisma-client-js"
  binaryTargets = ["native", "rhel-openssl-3.0.x", "debian-openssl-3.0.x"]
}

datasource db {
  provider = "postgresql"
  url      = env("DATABASE_URL")
}
